nodes.goal:
Census the in-scope files under {run.scan_root} for this standing rule:
{run.audit_rule}
List UP TO 40 candidate files the rule clearly applies to (skip vendored/generated paths unless the rule names them). PATHS ONLY in your answer - never file contents, never diffs, never quotes beyond one short reason. Reply with ONLY fenced json {"items": [{"path": "<absolute path>", "reason": "<why in scope, <= 80 chars>"}], "count": <int, must equal items length>, "notes": "<anything deliberately excluded and why>"}

fanout.goal:
Audit EXACTLY ONE file against the standing rule:
{run.audit_rule}
Your file: {item.path} (census picked it because: {item.reason}). Read the whole file with your tools - do not judge from a path name, an injected excerpt, or a diff. Judge the rule as written; if the rule does not cover something you saw, that is a pass with an observation, not a fail. Reply with ONLY fenced json {"path": "{item.path}", "finding": "<one line grounded in what you read, citing line numbers>", "pass": <bool>}
